Files containing derived code carry a header saying so and describing what was
changed, as Apache-2.0 section 4(b) requires. At the time of writing:

  crates/octane-sandbox/src/bwrap.rs
      The bubblewrap mount ordering and flag recipe — the order in which
      `--ro-bind`, `--tmpfs`, `--dev`, `--bind` and the `--unshare-*` flags must
      be applied for the resulting confinement to be correct — is derived from
      codex-rs/linux-sandbox/src/bwrap.rs. The code is a reimplementation
      against octane's own `SandboxPolicy`, not a copy.

  crates/octane-session/src/lib.rs
      The on-disk shape — an append-only JSONL file per session whose first
      line is metadata and whose remaining lines are conversation items, so a
      session killed mid-write stays readable up to its last complete line — is
      taken from codex-rs/rollout/src/recorder.rs. No code was copied; octane
      records its own `Message` type and has no index, database, or archive
      tier.

  crates/octane-tui/src/render.rs
      The shape of the diff renderer — a right-aligned line-number column, a
      coloured sign column beside syntax-highlighted content, the language
      inferred from the `+++ b/<path>` header's extension, the lexer restarted
      per hunk rather than carried across one, and a dim overlay marking the
      removed side — is derived from codex-rs/tui/src/diff_render.rs. No code
      was copied; octane highlights through its own `Highlighter` and palette,
      and dims removals where codex tints their background.

  crates/octane-tui/src/composer.rs
      The word-boundary rule for the composer's word motions and word deletions
      — the `WORD_SEPARATORS` set, and the rule that a run of those separators
      forms a word of its own so that deleting through `foo::bar()` removes
      `()`, then `bar`, then `::` — is derived from
      codex-rs/tui/src/bottom_pane/textarea.rs (`is_word_separator`,
      `split_word_pieces`). No code was copied: octane classifies characters
      directly rather than splitting on UAX #29 word bounds, so it carries no
      dependency on `unicode-segmentation`.

  crates/octane-tui/src/markdown.rs
      The way a pipe table is presented — cells padded to a measured column
      width, columns separated by a two-space gutter rather than drawn borders,
      the delimiter row becoming a rule under the header, and the last column
      left unpadded — is derived from codex-rs/tui/src/markdown_render.rs. No
      code was copied, and codex's width-allocation machinery (column
      classification, iterative shrinking, key/value fallback) is deliberately
      not taken: octane's renderer is not given a viewport width, so columns
      keep their natural width and the transcript wraps an over-wide table like
      any other long line.

